    "data": {
      "text": "E.Abinesh vs Tamil Nadu Government Rep. By on 23 February,\n2024\nAuthor: M.Dhandapani\nBench: M.Dhandapani\n Crl.O.P.(MD)\n Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court\n Dated: 23.02.2024\n Coram:\n The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Dhandapani\n Crl.O.P.(MD) No.5451 of 2022\n and Crl.M.P(MD).No.3848 of 2022\n E.Abinesh \n Vs.\n Tamil Nadu Government Rep.by \n S.Rajkumar,\n Food and Safety Officer,\n Thanjavur Town-1,\n Thanjavur District.  ...Re  PRAYER: Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 482 of  Cr.P.C, to call for the records pertaining to the proceedings in  S.T.C.No.867/2016 on the file of the learned Judicial Magistrate No  Thanjavur and quash the same against the petitioner. \n For petitioner : No-appearance  For Respondent : Mr.S.Manikandan  Government Advocat  ORDER When the matter was taken up for hearing on 21.02.2024, there was no representation for the petitioner. Hence, the matter was directed https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis to be listed under the caption for dismissal today. Today also, there is no representation for the petitioner. Hence, this Criminal Original Petition is dismissed for non-prosecution. Connected miscellaneous petition is closed. \nE.Abinesh vs Tamil Nadu Government Rep. By on 23 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/13986971/\n1 23.02.2024 Index : Yes/No Internet : Yes/No ssb https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis To 1.Tamil Nadu Government Rep.by S.Rajkumar, Food and Safety Officer, Thanjavur Town-1,\nThanjavur District. \n2.The Additional Public Prosecutor, Madurai Bench of Madras High Court, Madurai. \nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis M.DHANDAPANI. J.\nssb 23.02.2024 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis E.Abinesh vs Tamil Nadu Government Rep. By on 23 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/13986971/\n2",
